# strings3 — SET ... NX: only if it does not exist yet
#
# Learn: SET key value NX writes only when the key is absent and replies
# (nil) otherwise. It's the building block for locks and "first writer
# wins" logic, and it's atomic: no GET-then-SET race.
#
# Task: you are worker-b. Claim the locks for the "report" and "invoice"
# jobs, but never steal a lock another worker already holds. The check
# runs this against different sets of existing locks.
#

SET lock:report worker-b
SET lock:invoice worker-b
